COMPILATION OF: E46N13

D: Disk Print
L: List Source Program

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 1

   NO ERROR(S) IN PASS 2

PL/I-80 V1.4 COMPILATION OF: E46N13

   1 a 0000 E46N13:
   2 a 0006   procedure options(main);
   3 a 0006   /* [E2E-42/P2c] RUNTIME: FILE SKIP WITH A LIST, spelled
   4 a 0006      exactly as CREATE:44 spells it.  The item follows the
   5 a 0006      skip INSIDE one statement, so the question is whether
   6 a 0006      the skip's bytes come before the item's text. */
   7 c 0006   dcl outf file;
   8 c 0006   open file(outf) stream output title('N13OUT DAT');
   9 c 0023   put file(outf) skip list('EOF');
  10 c 0042   close file(outf);
  11 c 0048   stop;
  12 a 004B end E46N13;

CODE SIZE = 004B
DATA AREA = 000D
FREE SYMS = 3896
END  COMPILATION
